      "claim": "The Context/Problem narrative's file:line citations into saffron/cli.py, saffron/task.py and saffron/cell/session.py are wrong, pervasively, while every citation into CLAUDE.md, README.md, DESIGN.md, docs/appendices/H-what-v0-found.md, saffron/preflight.py, saffron/phases/package.py, saffron/cell/runtime.py and tests/test_cli.py lands exactly or within a line or two. Specific wrong pointers: saffron/cli.py:457-461 (actual token check is at line 502), saffron/cli.py:1611-1617 for _mirror_path (the function is defined at 1709 and called at 1298/1912; 1611-1617 is an unrelated comment), saffron/cli.py:302-309 and :453-476 for the dispatcher's except Exception -> exit 2 (the real handler is at 314-321; 453-476 is unrelated git-ancestry code), saffron/cli.py:110-236 for the full subcommand list (serve is actually defined at 242), saffron/task.py:654-668 for \"writes READY_FOR_REVIEW and re-raises\" (the actual write+raise is at 670-674), saffron/task.py:671 for \"the print after PACKAGE\" (the print is at 684), saffron/cell/session.py:1057-1060 and :1095-1111/:1096-1106 for the remove-before-create and host-probe pattern (the real code is at roughly 1084-1090 and 1116-1136), and saffron/cell/session.py:1897 for the scratch-network/saffron-cells subnet-sharing fact (line 1897 is an unrelated import; the real naming is at runtime.py:161-166 and session.py:1922). git log shows saffron/cli.py and saffron/task.py each received substantial edits from SA-0264, SA-0265 and SA-0266, which plausibly shifted these line numbers after the spec's citations were taken, and the stated source commit 0def7c4d does not exist anywhere in this repository's history so it cannot be used to double check. The functional claims attached to these wrong citations mostly hold up once the real code is located, so no acceptance criterion or witness depends on an exact line number, but a builder following the citations literally would open and copy the wrong neighboring code, especially for the probe/remove-before-create pattern in session.py that criteria 1 and 4 rely on.",
